{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an rna_only model with singleprofile settings and no aggregation, comparing it to the higher-performing multiprofile setup (config_003). Validation accuracy (0.4849) and F1 (0.4639) are lower than the multiprofile baseline, suggesting that multiprofile configurations may contribute more to performance than singleprofile settings or aggregation in this context. Uncertainty remains about the relative importance of profile configuration versus aggregation, and whether fusion strategies or alternative encoders could improve results."
}

